{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"30e8e41e5ab44c4e1c92faebc0aa2a6ead56ffc0a63dbf3043d95b85ca2a94ea","digest":{"component_or_area":"module-size gate CI workflows","key_entities":[".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml",".github/workflows/test.yml",".github/module-size-allowlist.txt","reconcile.py","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","listed=$(grep -vE '^[[:space:]]*(#|$)' \"$allowlist\" | awk '{print $1}' | sort -u)"],"problem_keywords":["grep-exit-failure","shell-pipefail","module-size-gate","allowlist-empty","ci-workflow"],"propositions":["The module-size gate shell step fails with exit 1 when the allowlist is fully drained (empty of non-comment lines) because grep returns exit 1 on no match, which aborts the step under bash -e -o pipefail before the over-cap check executes","Both .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml and .github/workflows/test.yml contain an identical unguarded grep command that needs to be wrapped with `|| true` to tolerate empty allowlists","The fix requires adding `{ grep -vE '^[[:space:]]*(#|$)' \"$allowlist\" || true; }` in place of the bare grep to allow the gate to complete and print 'Module-size gate: OK' on empty allowlists","The module-size gate must continue to fail (exit 1) when a non-allow-listed file exceeds 800 LOC, preserving gate behavior for non-empty allowlists"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787703912616425001,"uuid":"f874227f-9b72-44ff-9293-b703a0b505b9"}